      "writtenOn": "2026-03-23T22:00:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "driveby question: why doesn\u0027t this set `isNormalized \u003d false` also? Aren\u0027t they basically the same just with a different channel?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 73,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "935b695bb9491730ed230b2fea8108664a3a8ba1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a391edb_8bb9b1ac",
        "filename": "src/gpu/ganesh/GrDataUtils.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-24T02:34:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that that is a tricky question and I don\u0027t necessarily know if the current behavior is \"correct\", but this is to match `SkColorTypeIsNormalized`.  Alpha is presumed to be [0,1] or it doesn\u0027t make sense, whereas R,G,B can have valid negative or wide gamut \u003e 1 values that make sense depending on the color space.  The assumption in `SkColorTypeIsNormalized` is that even if the format can hold these extended range values, that alpha will be in [0,1]. \n\nI said \"correct\" because there\u0027s no real way we enforce that.",
      "parentUuid": "cef6add4_03ad808d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 73,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 82
      },
      "revId": "935b695bb9491730ed230b2fea8108664a3a8ba1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
