      "writtenOn": "2026-03-24T02:34:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It has to do with how the driver interprets the texture format and provides default RGBA values in a `sample()` call. In a red texture format, it implicity is \"r001\". GL_LUMINANCE is more like gray, so it sets its value into r,g, and b so we need wipe that out to act like red.",
      "parentUuid": "b3833730_9c4497bf",
